 # Global Index Map (Vertex)
 ## Overview
-The Global Index Map (Vertex) maps a local vertex identifier within a single hypertree to a unique global integer index across the entire hypertree grid object [S1, unofficial]. It aggregates sparse, variable-size hypertree structures into a single contiguous addressing space for visualization and property storage [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from the Hypertree Global Index Map, which identifies hypertrees themselves, by operating at the vertex level within a hypertree [S1, unofficial].
